  "notes": [
    "De-identified by kissflow-forge-eval/spikes/deidentify_template.py (that repo -- REAL tenant content, never committed here) from a real production process template. 5 QueryDefinition nodes were stripped (they carried prod-tenant-specific list/user dataset ids); the 2 Reference fields and 3 User fields they belonged to are converted to plain Text here, each Name flagged with a TODO pointing at shapes/field_user_reference.json (the proven User-field shape) and docs/capabilities/process-template.md.",
    "Permission/Resource/Component/Property/Criteria/Condition/Expression/Node were all dropped outright -- in-flight state, branch/validation AST, and a Reference-field UI widget config, none of it part of an identity SHELL structure. Re-add them per this repo's own CLAUDE.md Build order (members -> assignees -> visibility -> events) on TOP of a from_template clone, never by assuming this shape already carries them.",
    "A minimal 3-activity Start/UserTask(\"Manager Approve\")/End scaffold -- same shape family as shapes/process_skeleton.json, but pre-loaded with the real identity/initiate field block instead of a bare single placeholder step. The source template's suspended duplicate \"Manager Approve\" Activity and its SendBackToInitiator sibling are both dropped.",
    "Every Field's real display Name (mostly non-English in the source capture) is replaced with a generic English placeholder -- the \"template identity block\" this ticket asks for. A lone RichText info-banner column (real non-English text embedding a real prod URL) and its now-empty hosting Row were dropped explicitly during de-identification, never copied here.",
    "The source capture's own root Model had NO Model::Appearance key at all -- only 4 Column-level Appearance/Style pairs (the OPTIONAL per-section colour chain). A 5th, Model-level pair is synthesized here (Appearance_Sample05/Style_Sample04) to satisfy this repo's own proven Node-graph invariant that every flow needs the MANDATORY chain or the builder fails to render -- not copied from the source, which plausibly never had this gap caught because nobody opens a \"Duplicate me\" utility template directly.",
    "Ids are minted <Kind>_SampleNN, numbered per-kind -- kfforge.graph.clone_template_shell re-mints ALL of them again at clone time (kfforge.pages._instantiate, the same machinery nav.py already reuses from pages.py) so two from_template=True processes never collide.",
    "KF_PROCESS_TEMPLATE (env var) or an explicit template_path argument overrides which shapes/*.json file clone_template_shell loads -- this shipped shell is only the DEFAULT; a tenant-specific template belongs in tenant config, never hardcoded into the engine."
  ]
